<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36984" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pompĭlĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a
			Roman</i> gens. The most celebrated is Numa Pompilius, <i>the second king of Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1,
				12, 34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 2, 69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 1,
			18</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pom-pĭlĭus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Pompilius</i>, <i>Pompilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguis,</span>”
				i.e. <i>descendants of Numa Pompilius</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 292</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pompĭlĭānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>Pompilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curia,</span>”
				<i>built by Numa</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Vop. Aur. 41</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indigitamenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 95</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>